INSTALL
-------

git clone https://github.com/dickmao/epkg.git
make -C epkg install


USAGE
-----

- See samples/Makefile and samples/.github/workflows/ci.yml.

- Your Makefile must contain the top boilerplate:

include epkg.mk
epkg.mk:
	emacs --batch -l package -f package-initialize -l epkg -f epkg-copy-mk

- Three make variables must be defined:

  EPKG_FILES are relative paths to all files to be installed.
  EPKG_MAIN is the relative path containing the package headers.
  EPKG_TEST_EL are relative paths to ert tests.

- A make target named "install" must be defined.


DEPENDING ON AN EPKG-MADE PACKAGE
---------------------------------

Do not add its symbol to Package-Requires.  Instead,

(epkg-require 'your-package "https://github.com/you/your-package")


BRIEF EXEGESIS ON EPKG.LOCK
---------------------------

epkg.lock is automatically maintained to reflect the epkg-made
dependencies you *actually* used for testing.  It is automatically git
added to your repository.  If two subpackages lock to different commit
hashes of a common dependency, and one hash is the ancestor of the
other, then the latter gets locked.  If the hashes are from different
branches, then error.

The default commit of a dependency is the default branch tip.  To
lower it,

make epkg-get PKG=dependency REV=129d264 (for example)


TAXONOMY
--------

┌───────────────┬───────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┐
│ Subrole       │ Status Quo                │ Epkg                             │
├───────────────┼───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
│ Sourcing      │ elpa, nongnu-elpa,        │ git forges, e.g., GitHub         │
│               │ elpa-devel, nongnu-devel, │                                  │
│               │ melpa, melpa-stable       │                                  │
├───────────────┼───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
│ Versioning    │ unserious                 │ git commit hashes                │
├───────────────┼───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
│ Naming        │ first come, first taken   │ url paths, e.g.,                 │
│               │                           │ github.com/dickmao/emacs-ghostty │
├───────────────┼───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
│ Sandbox &     │ community staleware:      │ make target                      │
│ test          │ Eldev, Cask               │                                  │
├───────────────┼───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
│ Build         │ bespoke user elisp upon   │ make target                      │
│               │ first invocation          │                                  │
└───────────────┴───────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┘
